Hello Replit team,

Ahead of Web Summit Lisbon, we have written a page about Replit on PrompTugal.news:
https://promptugal.news/companies/replit/

It follows Replit at the summit: "Making useful intelligence accessible to everyone", Tuesday 10 November at 14:00, and 2 more sessions on the page.

One section is still empty: Replit's flows, how work moves through your product and where AI agents act in it. We map them only from public pages and never guess, so a few lines from you would get it right faster.

PrompTugal.news is a new newsroom from Portugal, for Europe, with one aim: to map the universe of AI in Portugal and the companies that come to it. Every fact on the page carries its source and the date we read it; if anything is wrong, reply and we correct it, dated.

The page also asks the three questions we ask every company: what your AI agents can reach, what they are authorised to do, and who controls the gap between the two. Could we hear your answer in 15 minutes during the summit, 9 to 12 November? Answering is optional, and two lines in writing are as welcome as a call. If you would rather talk than publish, we can just talk. Reply with a time that suits you.

Best regards,
Indi Gupte
Editor, PrompTugal.news

The team that makes PrompTugal.news also works on RiskMandate, so we are independent of Web Summit, not of RiskMandate; our disclosure says it in full: https://promptugal.news/about/participant.html

